### Spec First API — manual request collection
#
# For the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client). Open this
# file, then click "Send Request" above each block (or use the extension's
# keyboard shortcut) - requests run top to bottom, and later ones reuse the
# token/event id captured from earlier responses via {{name.response.body...}}.
#
# Prerequisites:
#   make dev-db && make migrate-up && make run-backend
# (see README.md - the API listens on @baseUrl below by default)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@email = demo@example.com
@password = password123
@name = Demo User

### Register a new user
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "name": "{{name}}"
}

### Log in and get a JWT
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### List events (global list - any authenticated user sees every event, not just their own)
GET {{baseUrl}}/events
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Create an event
# @name createEvent
POST {{baseUrl}}/events
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Backyard BBQ",
  "date": "2026-10-04T18:00:00Z",
  "location": "12 Elm St"
}

### List events again - the one just created should be there
GET {{baseUrl}}/events
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Add a guest to the event just created
POST {{baseUrl}}/events/{{createEvent.response.body.$.id}}/guests
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sam Rivera",
  "email": "sam@example.com"
}

### List guests for that event
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/{{createEvent.response.body.$.id}}/guests
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
